# K03 S7: `merge(((Model Other)))` has one operand -- P0 makes the sole container transparent once, and what it holds,
# the group `(Model Other)`, holds two items and no one value: an anonymous Structure, refused at the operand as a form
# no merge lowers yet, with no merge-specific flattening of nested groups.
Model:
    int: v 1
end: Model
Other:
    int: w 2
end: Other
fn: m () int
    A: merge(((Model Other)))
    return: A\v + A\w + 4
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
